        "reported_material_gaps": [],
        "research_rationale": "Identity: the census register lists EO 6331-E dated 1933-10-11 (Franklin D. Roosevelt); the WPA 1944 list entry for 1933 Oct 11, p.543, records the code for the Throwing Industry as approved, and the held text's date and subject agree. APP page check passed: the mirror page record with the held text's sha256 (common-crawl capture) has a heading naming this order's number, the same date and subject, and a text_sha256 equal to the held text's. The held text was read in full. Own terms: the order has no stated period, condition, \"until\" date, \"pending\" or provisional wording. Repeal route per the reviewed shared analysis: an approval under section 3 depended on the code approval and enforcement provisions that section 2 of S.J. Res. 113 repealed on June 14, 1935; Schechter (May 27, 1935) is recorded only as a validity characterization.\nMember checks: {\"earlier_end_check\":\"No held record shows this code cancelled, modified under section 10(b) in a way that replaces it, suspended or superseded before June 14, 1935: the census register, the WPA 1944 list and a code-name search of the held order texts (jobs/*/output/texts) were checked, and the machine searches (current-law:usc, current-law:ecfr, later-events:ofr_catalog) have no hit for this order; the OFR catalog starts in 1937 and is not adequate alone, and a code-name search can miss an order that names the code in other words. Held EO 6204-B (July 14, 1933) earlier approved in part certain provisions of a code for the same industry pending a hearing; it precedes this order and is not an end of it. No held later order names the Throwing Industry code. June 16, 1935 is not an end: section 1 of S.J. Res. 113 replaced the two-year expiry with April 1, 1936, and nothing in the resolution defers section 2.\",\"independent_command_check\":\"No appointment, delegation, committee, report direction or other command independent of the code appears; \\\"Approval recommended: Hugh S. Johnson, Administrator\\\" is a recommendation, not a command.\",\"savings_check\":\"Savings source SUPPLEMENT:SJRES113 (with SUPPLEMENT:NIRA5 for the section 5 text) read; accrued acts, liabilities and the section 5 exemption for completed action survive only as accrued effects; no held source shows a prosecution or enforcement continued after June 14, 1935, and none continues this approval.\",\"scope_check\":\"The order has one operative command, the approval of the code: \\\"do adopt and approve the report, recommendations and findings of the Administrator and do order that the said code of fair competition be and it is hereby approved.\\\" The inventory is a single whole-order clause and was confirmed against the full text; the recitals describe the application, hearings and the Administrator's findings and command nothing.\"}",
